This is the workaround I found for now:
1. create a function to change a dynamic tool into a normal tool
```
function convertToNormalTools(
tools: Record<string, Tool>,
): Record<string, Tool> {
const result = Object.fromEntries(
Object.entries(tools).map(([name, tool]) => {
const { type, ...rest } = tool; // remove type=dynamic from mcp tools
return [
name,
{
...rest,
},
];
}),
);
return result;
}
```
1. wrap the mcp tools with the funciton
```
const mcpTools = convertToNormalTools(await mcpClient.tools());
```
This makes the addToolResult work again.
...
I found a way to work around this.
you can using the `tool` function wrap your mcp tool.
like this
```
tools: {
yourTool: tool({ description: yourMcpTool.description, inputSchema: yourMcpTool.inputSchema })
}
```

